{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932741-cofd-and-sanity-system-like-in-call-of-cthulhu","id":932741,"title":"CofD and Sanity system like in Call of Cthulhu?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-16T19:46:39-07:00","id":932741,"title":"CofD and Sanity system like in Call of Cthulhu?","content":"CofD and Sanity system like in Call of Cthulhu?<br /> <br /> I really like the sanity system in Call of Cthulhu, its the only thing that is missing for me in the system. How can it be done with D10's and incorporated into the system?<br /> <br /> PS: Why are there no CofD storytellers screen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>/Brian","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10532-bergh","name":"Bergh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:47:29-07:00","id":932743,"title":"","content":"Integrity is basically the same thing as Sanity though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T20:07:47-07:00","id":932752,"title":"","content":"The lack of ST screens is because the CofD material isn't done with traditional print runs, and their PoD service doesn't do printed screens at the moment.<br /> <br /> They do ST screens for the Kickstarter based games, and some of them have a digital file you can print out for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T20:15:41-07:00","id":932757,"title":"","content":"Integrity is already a thing in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T04:10:18-07:00","id":932862,"title":"","content":"My group used to run it Resolve + Composure x 10 (or if your group are more masochistic, x5) and then roll against it as d100. Yeah, it's not exactly smooth, but then CoC before the more recent edition was pretty messy so no one noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:34:04-07:00","id":932980,"title":"","content":"Has no relation to integrity. And it's a good idea. Very well developed in Mirrors and properly explained the correlation using both integrity as sanity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:53:50-07:00","id":932985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932741-cofd-and-sanity-system-like-in-call-of-cthulhu?p=932980#post932980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has no relation to integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Both track a character's ability to cope with experiencing the traumatic and the supernaturally horrifying. Both cause negative psychological effects when lost. The main differences I see are mechanical, but narratively speaking they fill the same niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932741-cofd-and-sanity-system-like-in-call-of-cthulhu?p=932980#post932980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's a good idea. Very well developed in Mirrors and properly explained the correlation using both integrity as sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Impressive that Mirrors managed to do that before the Integrity system was even written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-17-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T12:03:29-07:00","id":932990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932741-cofd-and-sanity-system-like-in-call-of-cthulhu?p=932985#post932985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? Both track a character's ability to cope with experiencing the traumatic and the supernaturally horrifying. Both cause negative psychological effects when lost. The main differences I see are mechanical, but narratively speaking they fill the same niche.<br /> <br /> <br /> Impressive that Mirrors managed to do that before the Integrity system was even written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity is the ancient refined humanity system. The rules of the Health Mirrors are not canceled nor the texts explaining the correlations between the two systems, one of morality and other sanity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T12:21:15-07:00","id":932994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/932741-cofd-and-sanity-system-like-in-call-of-cthulhu?p=932990#post932990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity is the ancient refined humanity system. The rules of the Health Mirrors are not canceled nor the texts explaining the correlations between the two systems, one of morality and other sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the narrative role Integrity has nothing to do with morality. The shared mechanical framework is where the similarities begin and end, and narratively Integrity is far closer to Sanity than it is to Morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud